{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are on a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/9596b5a2993d0f1ce48e542106bde5b216018861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of the minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. What is the length of the line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a120efd2fb6e7261a78f8962f82e20cccf62ba7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\sqrt {10} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac {7}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt {14} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt {15} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"428\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the angle that subtends the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. By the law of cosines,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2cc0e94690429f98559b390b4942de4d2d3ca920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2=5^2+5^2-2\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cos(\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"19\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/062039b2a7f76a9ac40862a85ba9fad0d7d8dd74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\alpha) = 7/25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities#Half_Angle_Identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\"> half-angle formula</a> says that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85734339a5e0cebf841cfdee30d16aa04890c62b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\alpha/2) = \\frac{\\sqrt{1+\\cos(\\alpha)}}{2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{32/25}{2}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"387\" height=\"44\" />. The law of cosines tells us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046b1e34ca0071d9191d219144ae1c99e49fa40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{5^2+5^2-2\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}} = \\sqrt{50-50\\frac{4}{5}} = \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"399\" height=\"43\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79e0e8ce41b5c08729443bcc258d13ca061ff35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as the midpoint of line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the center of the circle. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8e334863383e1304e64c7c4b51cc7c26685ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ODA=90\\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecd101b6c2c77868420ee0455c332846d5b4058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD=\\sqrt{5^2-3^2}=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60db66b3eb0599603ec8bb64aacf34269b88291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f560ec4cefd1167823d5ffea2c025cfcee5990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=5-4=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/061de056542e64695f2646f3a9ca3c02efe324bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\sqrt{3^2+1^2}=\\sqrt{10} \\rightarrow \\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"232\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72fbe8b90fcde66500984b26ba2b38b0f7765119.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pen d = linewidth(0.7); pathpen = d; pointpen = black; pen f = fontsize(9); path p = CR((0,0),5); pair O = (0,0), A=(5,0), B = IP(p,CR(A,6)), C = IP(p,CR(A,3)), D=IP(A--B,O--C); D(p); D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A,E)--D(MP(&quot;O&quot;,O))--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,NE)--cycle); D(A--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,ENE),dashed+d); D(O--C,dashed+d); D(rightanglemark(O,D(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D,W)),A)); MP(&quot;5&quot;,(A+O)/2); MP(&quot;3&quot;,(A+D)/2,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"652\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitab